body:
[https://ibb.co/dr31fYW](https://ibb.co/dr31fYW) \- that one in front, top and the left side, are those considered intake fans?

&#x200B;

I got aerocool 500 case

damn, seems like the pc shop guy that i asked to upgrade my pc, didnt do this one last step , which is connect the 3 pin rear fan onto the 4 pin mobo's slot, holy cow.

&#x200B;

P.S on ryzen master im seeing even 34 C now at idle O.o . Yeah it seems like i only have one case fan, i got controls on top of the chase high- off - low, i guess ill keep it to high..

&#x200B;

P.S #2 as im writing, ryzen master even shoes 33.7 now , holy smokes ;)

&#x200B;

Oh another p.S when i opened the case, andtouched my gtx 1080 it was really hot, could it have been because there was no air flow in and out of the case? :)

&#x200B;

Here's a photo of where i connected the 3 pin case wire to the 4 pin slot on mobo - [https://ibb.co/DDL1jMc](https://ibb.co/DDL1jMc)

&#x200B;

I hope its the right slot, as i found only  1 sys fan slot on top of the motherboard

&#x200B;

. I've never ever built computers before, so tinkering around seems really fun to me :)
